          "reason": "The unit contains a minor conceptual error regarding how atoms combine during chemical reactions.",
          "errors": [
            {
              "passage_ids": [
                "p27"
              ],
              "description": "The passage claims that atoms combine in integer numbers of moles ('les atomes se combinent en nombre entier de moles'). In reality, atoms combine in integer ratios of individual atoms/particles, which translates macroscopically to fixed molar ratios (stoichiometric ratios); chemical reactions do not require integer quantities of moles.",
